You are working on NoteFlow, an Expo SDK 54 React Native app written in TypeScript.

Stack:
- Expo Router for all navigation.
- Gluestack UI v5 alpha concepts with UniWind and local design tokens.
- Shopify FlashList for all long lists.
- Zustand for global state.
- AsyncStorage through Zustand persist for local persistence.
- Zod for form validation.
- React Native Reanimated for list animations.
- Expo Haptics for tactile feedback.

Project structure:
- app/ contains file-based routes.
- components/ contains reusable UI, cards, details and common screens.
- constants/theme.ts contains visual tokens.
- store/notesStore.ts contains all persisted global note state.
- types/index.ts contains domain types and type guards.
- docs/ contains project documentation.

Coding rules:
- Use functional components and hooks.
- Keep state local with useState when it belongs to one screen.
- Use Zustand selectors for global state. Do not add Context API for notes.
- Do not replace FlashList with FlatList or ScrollView for tab lists.
- Keep Date fields as Date objects in app code and rehydrate persisted dates.
- Validate creation forms with Zod before writing to the store.
- Respect light and dark themes from useColorScheme.
- Use @expo/vector-icons for icons.
- Keep UI native; do not use WebView for app screens.
- Prefer small, focused components and explicit TypeScript types.
